+
+## Detached search execution
+
+Frame prepares a `PreparedBrowserSearch` under its store mutex, executes provider,
+reranker and optional synthesis I/O without that mutex, and finishes the opaque
+`CompletedBrowserSearch` under the mutex. The original `programmable_search`
+entry point uses the same phases for existing callers. Query context is a
+snapshot; later captures and profile changes affect subsequent queries. Index
+leases protect active generations from pruning, including temporary roots.
+Completion is bound to the originating store, and retained sessions preserve the
+existing persistence and bounded-cache semantics (ordered by completion).
+The focused regression covers out-of-order completion, capture during a query,
+generation reclamation, and rejection by a different store with the same label.
